From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] UB-128: opt-in stale and wholly overwritten texture uploads, safe a frame ahead

Port of EdGlantine-PS5 df66705be6 / 99zzzz3-skip-stale-texture-uploads.diff.
EDEN_UP_SKIP_STALE_UPLOADS=1 (Common::PeSwitch, exact 1, first use) enables our
existing stale-page protocol and a corrected whole-alias-copy decision. Reuse
StalePages, ClearStaleGpu and StaleNx2MayBeGpuWritten: this tree already has the
original buffer-written bitmap, so it needs no GpuWrittenPages replacement.

Two fixes over the first draft, both only with the switch on:

1. A frame run ahead (EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1), a guest write W can be applied
   (GatherAndApply -> OnCacheInvalidations -> WriteMemory) before an older image A's
   draws: A uploads W, is drawn over, the collector drops it and MarkStale marked its
   pages, so the next image at those pages skipped its upload and showed undefined
   data while guest memory held W, the newest bytes. New ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes:
   set in RefreshContents once an image goes on to take guest bytes (now, by layer,
   or by a queued decode or unswizzle) and in WriteMemory when a CPU write lands on
   a live image (a full clear that drops the upload still leaves W in guest memory).
   MarkStale refuses an image carrying it, counted (tc_stale_refused). The flag is
   never cleared: refusing a mark only costs an upload later, never a picture.
   Sparse layer, sparse tile, unwritten sparse and remapped images are refused too.
   Round 2: a joined image made without RefreshContents (whole alias copy, full
   clear, StaleUploadOverDrawnTarget) lost the flag. A new image now takes it from
   every alias and overlap in join_copies_to_do, from every overlap it replaces
   (join_ignore_textures) and, on the StaleUploadOverDrawnTarget path, from the
   drawn bad overlaps it stands in for (tc_guest_bytes_joined). With
   EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1 (read as nx2_gsv.h reads it: unset -1, a value starting
   with '1' is 1, else 0) MarkStale marks nothing (tc_stale_ahead_refused): that
   also covers a write W that lands on pages with no live image.

2. The whole-alias-copy rule checked copy geometry only (CopiesWriteWholeImage), but
   CopyImage copies the source's host image as it is, with no RefreshContents or
   PrepareImage: a source with a pending upload (CpuModified, dirty layers) or a
   decode or unswizzle still queued (IsDecoding, async_decodes) handed the new image
   old bytes. Such a copy now counts as partial and the upload stays
   (tc_whole_copy_stale_src); taken ones are counted (tc_whole_copy_skips).

The whole-copy path still rejects scaling, compressed formats, partial coverage,
non-2D images, rescaled/trimmed/sparse/unbacked/remapped images and multisampling.
The counters go into the existing 600-frame texture cache log line.
Do not change old EDEN_NX2_SKIP_OVERWRITTEN_UPLOADS or EDEN_UP_NO_STALE_UPLOAD
behavior when the new switch is unset: the flag is only set with the switch on and
only read by MarkStale under it. No shader cache key or format changes.
See front-ub128.diff for the Vulkan frontend post-write-back hook (unchanged: the
front clears stale pages after a write-back; the flag needs nothing from the front).
Base: T88 core (patches through 0492) with 0493 and 0494; also applies without them.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/image_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/image_base.h
index 3c66304..33f26f0 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/image_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/image_base.h
@@ -62,6 +62,12 @@ enum class ImageFlagBits : u32 {
     /// device memory when the guest memory under it can hold data (Image::BindTiles), and only
     /// the parts written are uploaded.
     SparseTiles = 1 << 23,
+    /// EDEN_UP_SKIP_STALE_UPLOADS: guest memory under this image holds bytes the guest wrote
+    /// while the image existed (uploaded from there, or a CPU write landed on it). Run a frame
+    /// ahead, such a write can be applied before older draws into the image: the GPU's data is
+    /// then not the newest, so MarkStale leaves these pages alone. A new image joined from
+    /// others takes it from them (JoinImages). Never cleared; only set with the switch on.
+    GuestBytes = 1 << 24,
 };
 DECLARE_ENUM_FLAG_OPERATORS(ImageFlagBits)
 
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index 94a8500..8d60d99 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -495,6 +495,36 @@ void TextureCache<P>::MarkStale(const ImageBase& image) {
                             ImageFlagBits::Unbacked))) {
         return;
     }
+    if (SkipStaleUploads()) {
+        // UB-128, frames ahead: with EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1 nothing is marked at all. A guest
+        // write W can be applied before older draws, also to pages no live image covers (then
+        // no image carries GuestBytes for it), so the GPU's data is never known to be the
+        // newest. Read as nx2_gsv.h's PresentClientBuffer reads it (frames_ahead_setting):
+        // unset -1, a value starting with '1' is 1, anything else 0.
+        static const int frames_ahead_setting = [] {
+            const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD");
+            return value == nullptr ? -1 : value[0] == '1' ? 1 : 0;
+        }();
+        if (frames_ahead_setting >= 1) {
+            ++tc_stale_ahead_refused;
+            return;
+        }
+        // UB-128. Run a frame ahead (EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1), a guest write to these pages can
+        // be applied before this image's older draws: the image uploads it, is drawn over, and
+        // the GPU's data is not the newest after all. Guest memory then holds what the next
+        // image here must show, so an image that ever took guest bytes keeps its pages unmarked.
+        // A new image joined from others inherits the flag (JoinImages). Sparse layer, tile and
+        // remapped images are left out as well: their pages are not one plain range the next
+        // image can be checked against.
+        if (True(image.flags & (ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes | ImageFlagBits::SparseLayers |
+                                ImageFlagBits::SparseTiles | ImageFlagBits::UnwrittenSparse |
+                                ImageFlagBits::Remapped))) {
+            if (True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes)) {
+                ++tc_stale_refused;
+            }
+            return;
+        }
+    }
     // Tracked from here on so CPU writes reach WriteMemory. Marking before the image's own
     // tracking goes keeps the pages' write protection from switching off and on again.
     stale_pages.Mark(image.cpu_addr, image.guest_size_bytes, [this](DAddr addr, u64 size) {
@@ -1210,6 +1240,16 @@ void TextureCache<P>::TickFrame() {
                      (stale_pages.Count() << StalePages::STALE_PAGE_BITS) >> 20);
             tc_stale_skips = tc_stale_skip_bytes = tc_stale_gpu_written = 0;
         }
+        if (SkipStaleUploads()) {
+            LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
+                     "Texture cache last 600 frames: UB-128 marks refused {} (image holds guest "
+                     "bytes), {} (frames ahead), {} joined images took the guest bytes flag, "
+                     "whole alias copies {} skipped the upload, {} not taken (source not current)",
+                     tc_stale_refused, tc_stale_ahead_refused, tc_guest_bytes_joined,
+                     tc_whole_copy_skips, tc_whole_copy_stale_src);
+            tc_stale_refused = tc_stale_ahead_refused = tc_guest_bytes_joined = 0;
+            tc_whole_copy_skips = tc_whole_copy_stale_src = 0;
+        }
         images_uploaded = uploaded_bytes = largest_upload = layer_uploads = 0;
         astc_opaque_images = astc_alpha_images = 0;
         std::vector<std::pair<u32, u64>> shapes;
@@ -2385,6 +2425,11 @@ void TextureCache<P>::WriteMemory(DAddr cpu_addr, size_t size) {
         }
         // EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW: delta draws keep image views without preparing their images.
         VideoCommon::Nx2FastDraw::Break(VideoCommon::Nx2FastDraw::Reason::Invalidation);
+        if (SkipStaleUploads()) {
+            // UB-128: the guest wrote under this image. Even a full clear that drops the upload
+            // leaves these bytes in guest memory, so the image is never marked stale (MarkStale).
+            image.flags |= ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes;
+        }
         if (True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::SparseTiles)) {
             MarkRangeWritten(image, cpu_addr, size);
             return;
@@ -3274,7 +3319,9 @@ void TextureCache<P>::RefreshContents(Image& image, ImageId image_id) {
     // EDEN_UP_NO_STALE_UPLOAD: made where a dropped GPU-written image left stale bytes
     // (MarkStale): nothing to upload. Pages the buffer cache wrote on the GPU may hold data
     // written back since: upload those. Nothing is marked with the switch off.
+    // UB-128 (EDEN_UP_SKIP_STALE_UPLOADS) reuses this tracking; a remapped image is uploaded.
     if (stale_pages.Count() != 0 && Tegra::g_nx2_ampere.load(std::memory_order_relaxed) &&
+        (!SkipStaleUploads() || False(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::Remapped)) &&
         image.dirty_layers.empty() &&
         False(image.flags & (ImageFlagBits::Sparse | ImageFlagBits::SparseLayers |
                              ImageFlagBits::SparseTiles | ImageFlagBits::Unbacked)) &&
@@ -3287,6 +3334,12 @@ void TextureCache<P>::RefreshContents(Image& image, ImageId image_id) {
         }
         ++tc_stale_gpu_written;
     }
+    if (SkipStaleUploads()) {
+        // UB-128: from here on the host image takes guest bytes (now, by layer, or by a queued
+        // decode or unswizzle). Should the GPU draw over them, guest memory may still be the
+        // newer side when a frame runs ahead: MarkStale leaves this image's pages alone.
+        image.flags |= ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes;
+    }
 
     // Vectors, staging and unswizzle scratch, as for a whole image further down.
     try {
@@ -5050,6 +5103,27 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
         new_image.flags |= ImageFlagBits::Sparse;
     }
 
+    if (SkipStaleUploads()) {
+        // UB-128: three paths below make the new image without RefreshContents, which sets
+        // GuestBytes (a whole alias copy, a full clear, StaleUploadOverDrawnTarget). The new
+        // image holds what the images it joins held: it takes their flag, from every alias and
+        // overlap it copies and every overlap it replaces (join_ignore_textures), before those
+        // are deleted. Otherwise a frame run ahead, W taken by an old image could be marked
+        // stale through the new one (MarkStale).
+        const auto took_guest_bytes = [this](ImageId id) {
+            return True(slot_images[id].flags & ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes);
+        };
+        bool joined_guest_bytes = std::ranges::any_of(
+            join_copies_to_do, [&](const JoinCopy& copy) { return took_guest_bytes(copy.id); });
+        for (const ImageId overlap_id : join_ignore_textures) {
+            joined_guest_bytes |= took_guest_bytes(overlap_id);
+        }
+        if (joined_guest_bytes) {
+            new_image.flags |= ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes;
+            ++tc_guest_bytes_joined;
+        }
+    }
+
     for (const ImageId overlap_id : join_ignore_textures) {
         Image& overlap = slot_images[overlap_id];
         if (True(overlap.flags & ImageFlagBits::GpuModified)) {
@@ -5158,11 +5232,42 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
         const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_SKIP_OVERWRITTEN_UPLOADS");
         return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
     }();
+    // UB-128 (EDEN_UP_SKIP_STALE_UPLOADS=1): the whole-copy rule checks the copy geometry on a
+    // plain, unscaled, single-sample 2D image (CopiesWriteWholeImage), and the source's host image
+    // must be current: CopyImage below copies it as it is, with no RefreshContents, so a source
+    // with a pending upload (CpuModified, dirty layers) or a decode or unswizzle still queued
+    // (IsDecoding, async_decodes) would hand the new image old bytes. Such a copy counts as
+    // partial and the upload stays.
+    const auto whole_copy_source_current = [&](const AliasedImage& aliased) {
+        const Image& source = slot_images[aliased.id];
+        if (True(source.flags & (ImageFlagBits::CpuModified | ImageFlagBits::IsDecoding)) ||
+            !source.dirty_layers.empty() ||
+            std::ranges::any_of(async_decodes, [&](const auto& decode) {
+                return decode->image_id == aliased.id && !decode->cancelled;
+            })) {
+            ++tc_whole_copy_stale_src;
+            return false;
+        }
+        return true;
+    };
     size_t first_copy = 0;
     bool copied_whole = false;
-    for (size_t index = skip_overwritten_uploads ? join_copies_to_do.size() : 0; index-- > 0;) {
+    for (size_t index = (skip_overwritten_uploads || SkipStaleUploads())
+                            ? join_copies_to_do.size() : 0; index-- > 0;) {
         const AliasedImage* const aliased = alias_copy(join_copies_to_do[index]);
-        if (aliased != nullptr && writes_whole_image(*aliased)) {
+        if (aliased == nullptr) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        const bool whole = SkipStaleUploads()
+                               ? (!can_rescale &&
+                                  CopiesWriteWholeImage(new_image, slot_images[aliased->id],
+                                                        aliased->copies) &&
+                                  whole_copy_source_current(*aliased))
+                               : writes_whole_image(*aliased);
+        if (whole) {
+            if (SkipStaleUploads()) {
+                ++tc_whole_copy_skips;
+            }
             first_copy = index;
             copied_whole = true;
             break;
@@ -5220,6 +5325,15 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
         runtime.TransitionImageLayout(new_image);
     } else if (StaleUploadOverDrawnTarget(new_image, new_info)) {
         // What RefreshContents does, without the upload (as for copied_whole above).
+        if (SkipStaleUploads() && False(new_image.flags & ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes) &&
+            std::ranges::any_of(join_bad_overlap_ids, [this](ImageId id) {
+                return True(slot_images[id].flags & ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes);
+            })) {
+            // UB-128: this image replaces the same target at another size, a bad overlap (not
+            // in join_copies_to_do): it takes that overlap's GuestBytes flag too.
+            new_image.flags |= ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes;
+            ++tc_guest_bytes_joined;
+        }
         new_image.flags &= ~ImageFlagBits::CpuModified;
         if (False(new_image.flags & ImageFlagBits::Tracked)) {
             TrackImage(new_image, new_image_id);
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
index 757e149..2736eec 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
@@ -932,9 +932,18 @@ private:
     /// write-backs clear them. An image made entirely on marked pages starts without an upload:
     /// the upload would only copy stale bytes the GPU overwrites. Switch 2 titles only: the
     /// buffer cache feeds the GPU-written page bitmap for them alone. Off: nothing is marked.
+    /// UB-128 (EDEN_UP_SKIP_STALE_UPLOADS=1): the same tracking, a corrected whole-alias-copy
+    /// rule (CopiesWriteWholeImage, and only from a source whose host image is current), and
+    /// guards for a frame run ahead: with EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1 nothing is marked stale; else
+    /// an image that took guest bytes (ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes, inherited by a joined image)
+    /// is never marked stale, and sparse or remapped images are left out. Implies NoStaleUpload.
+    [[nodiscard]] static bool SkipStaleUploads() {
+        static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_SKIP_STALE_UPLOADS");
+        return enabled;
+    }
     [[nodiscard]] static bool NoStaleUpload() {
         static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_NO_STALE_UPLOAD");
-        return enabled;
+        return enabled || SkipStaleUploads();
     }
     void MarkStale(const ImageBase& image);
     void ClearStale(DAddr addr, size_t size);
@@ -945,6 +954,11 @@ private:
     u64 tc_stale_skips{};        ///< Uploads skipped (last 600 frames)
     u64 tc_stale_skip_bytes{};
     u64 tc_stale_gpu_written{};  ///< Stale but buffer-written pages: uploaded after all
+    u64 tc_stale_refused{};      ///< UB-128: marks refused, the image holds guest bytes
+    u64 tc_stale_ahead_refused{}; ///< UB-128: marks refused, EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1
+    u64 tc_guest_bytes_joined{}; ///< UB-128: new images that took GuestBytes from joined images
+    u64 tc_whole_copy_skips{};   ///< UB-128: uploads skipped, a whole alias copy writes the image
+    u64 tc_whole_copy_stale_src{}; ///< UB-128: whole copies not taken, the source is not current
 
     /// The CPU address an image at gpu_addr is keyed by: its backing, or a fixed stand-in.
     [[nodiscard]] std::optional<DAddr> ImageCpuAddress(GPUVAddr gpu_addr, size_t size) const;
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/util.cpp b/src/video_core/texture_cache/util.cpp
index 78a07d5..fdb8055 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/util.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/util.cpp
@@ -1507,6 +1507,39 @@ Extent3D MipBlockSize(const ImageInfo& info, u32 level) {
     return AdjustMipBlockSize(num_tiles, level_info.block, level, level_info.num_levels);
 }
 
+bool CopiesWriteWholeImage(const ImageBase& dst, const ImageBase& src,
+                           std::span<const ImageCopy> copies) {
+    constexpr ImageFlagBits excluded = ImageFlagBits::Rescaled | ImageFlagBits::TrimmedLevels |
+                                       ImageFlagBits::Unbacked | ImageFlagBits::Sparse |
+                                       ImageFlagBits::SparseLayers | ImageFlagBits::SparseTiles |
+                                       ImageFlagBits::UnwrittenSparse | ImageFlagBits::Remapped;
+    if (dst.info.type != ImageType::e2D || src.info.type != ImageType::e2D ||
+        src.info.num_samples != 1 || dst.info.num_samples != 1 ||
+        src.info.format != dst.info.format || src.info.astc_opaque != dst.info.astc_opaque ||
+        True((src.flags | dst.flags) & excluded)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    // Alias copies count a compressed extent in blocks, but the backends copy it as texels, so
+    // such a copy writes only part of the image.
+    if (DefaultBlockWidth(dst.info.format) != 1 || DefaultBlockHeight(dst.info.format) != 1) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    for (s32 level = 0; level < dst.info.resources.levels; ++level) {
+        const Extent3D size = MipSize(dst.info.size, level);
+        const bool covered = std::ranges::any_of(copies, [&](const ImageCopy& copy) {
+            return copy.dst_subresource.base_level == level &&
+                   copy.dst_subresource.base_layer == 0 &&
+                   copy.dst_subresource.num_layers >= dst.info.resources.layers &&
+                   copy.dst_offset == Offset3D{} && copy.extent.width >= size.width &&
+                   copy.extent.height >= size.height;
+        });
+        if (!covered) {
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+    return true;
+}
